<section class="example-section">
  <p>Traveling with bitcoin backups is one of the most nerve wrecking experiences for someone who cares about security. Specially when going through borders or airports.</p>
  <p>My recomendation is to not travel with metal backups at all and instead create them at the location you plan to store. But still you need to travel with some backup like paper. I recommend steganography which is essentially embedding and obfuscating information on other pieces of information. For example, writing down the encrypted backup as decimal numbers in a receipt where it looks like it is listing products along with prices. Since this is just meant for transport and since it is encrypted you can simply put this in your wallet and maybe an extra copy in your backpack or pocket that way when you reach your backup location you can transcribe it to metal and destroy the paper backup. If you think about it some more there are countless ways you can obfuscate the backup since it is just a few bytes.</p>
  <p>I honestly recommend you stay away from most main stream modes of border wallets that are simply not very good and use steganography instead.</p>

